 "help": "usage: wgsextract bam to-cram [-h] [-r REGION] [--gene GENE] [--cram-version {2.1,3.0,3.1}]\n                              [--mimalloc {auto,off}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region (e.g. chrM, chrY:10000-20000)\n  --gene GENE           Filter by Gene Name (e.g. BRCA1, KCNQ2)\n  --cram-version {2.1,3.0,3.1}\n                        CRAM version to output (default: 3.0 for better compatibility)\n  --mimalloc {auto,off}\n                        Windows CRAM 3.1: use the installed native mimalloc encoder (auto) or\n                        system allocator (off). Default: config mimalloc, else auto.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract bam to-cram --input sample.bam --ref hs38.fa\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>.cram (+ .crai).\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools, sambamba; minutes\n  on a 30x genome.\n",
